# Plan, scope, and finish green

## Plan first
- For any non-trivial task (3+ steps or ambiguous), write a short todo/plan and confirm scope
  before coding. Use Plan mode for large or ambiguous asks.
- Anything outside the agreed scope goes to `FEATURES.md` as deferred — don't build it now.

## Keep changes scoped
- One concern per branch/commit. Don't bundle unrelated features into one big change
  (past commits bundled 5+ things — unreviewable and un-bisectable).
- Commit working increments often; don't let large piles of work sit uncommitted.

## Ship every change (commit + push)
- After **any** code change — not only backlog tasks — **commit and push before you say done**
  (unless the user explicitly says not to commit or not to push).
- Do not leave local-only diffs across turns; unpushed work breaks the user's other machines,
  simulators, and CI.
- Flow: finish the change → `./scripts/dev.sh check` green → commit → `git push` → confirm push
  landed.

## One task, then merge, then continue
- When the user gives a multi-item backlog (e.g. refinement lanes, ticket lists), **finish one
  task completely** before starting the next — don't stack two lanes in one uncommitted batch.
- Only after that push lands start the next task.
- If a task grows mid-flight, stop and ask whether to split or defer — don't silently absorb
  the next item into the same diff.

## After a PR merges — no leftover Compare & pull request
GitHub shows **Compare & pull request** when a remote branch still has commits that are
not ancestors of `main`. Squash-merge does **not** make those SHAs ancestors. Extra pushes
onto that head after merge make it worse (`fix/mobile-math-no-gray-clip`,
`claude/pull-latest-code-*`).

- **Never push** to a branch whose PR is already merged or closed. New work → new branch
  from current `origin/main`.
- Merge with **delete the head branch** (`gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`). If the
  branch still exists, `git push origin --delete <branch>` before you say done.
- Cloud/agent branches (`claude/*`, `cursor/*`): when their unique work is on `main`,
  **delete the remote branch**. Do not keep pushing them.
- Unique commits still on a merged/closed head: cherry-pick onto a **new** branch from
  `origin/main`, open one PR, then delete the old branch. Do not revive the old head.
- Before ending a session that touched git: `gh pr list --state open` and
  `git fetch` + `git log origin/main..origin/<your-branch>`. If GitHub would offer
  Compare & pull request on a dead head, delete it.

## Definition of done (don't say "done" until this holds)
- Run the full gate locally: `./scripts/dev.sh check` (API: ruff + format + mypy + pytest ≥80%;
  mobile: typecheck + lint). It must be green.
- **Commit and push** — work is not done until the remote has the changes.
- CI order is ruff → format → mypy → pytest; an earlier failure means tests never run — so match
  the whole chain locally, not just pytest.
- Never weaken the gate to pass — no lowering the coverage bar, no blanket `# type: ignore` /
  `# noqa` — without saying so explicitly.
